   'time',
   'Leehan honors 1st Lt. Damon Leehan, who was killed by an improvised explosive device on Aug. 14, 2011, while on a mission in Afghanistan. CrossFit describes him as a devoted husband, father and citizen soldier who served two tours of duty. He was the 1,742nd soldier lost in Operation Enduring Freedom.

You complete 7 rounds of 6 deadlifts (185 lb / 125 lb), 6 air squats and 6 box jumps (24 in / 20 in). Then you finish with a 1,742 m row, a distance that matches his place as the 1,742nd soldier lost. The rounds are short, but 42 deadlifts tire your back and legs before the long row. A steady pace through the rounds leaves you strong enough to hold your split on the rower.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "7 rounds of 6", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs, and stand all the way up. Do the 6 in a row if you can.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "7 rounds of 6", "tip": "Hip crease below the knee and stand tall. These are a quick breath between the bar and the box."}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "7 rounds of 6", "tip": "Land softly with both feet on the box and stand up fully at the top. Step down to save your legs.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Row", "reps": "1,742 m", "tip": "Settle into a split you can hold. Drive with your legs first, then lean back and pull."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Keep the deadlifts unbroken while you can", "Step down from the box", "Save some energy for the 1,742 m row"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the barbell, the box and the rower close together so you lose no time moving between them.", "Brace and set a flat back before every deadlift, even when you are tired.", "Use the air squats to slow your breathing before the box jumps.", "Step down from each box jump rather than rebounding, which is easier on your Achilles tendons.", "On the row, pick a steady split for the first 500 m and push harder only in the last 500 m."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 135 lb / 95 lb or less. Use a 20 in / 16 in box or do box step-ups. Newer athletes can do 5 rounds and row 1,000 m.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Leehan workout?", "answer": "7 rounds for time of 6 deadlifts (185 lb / 125 lb), 6 air squats and 6 box jumps (24 in / 20 in), followed by a 1,742 m row."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Leehan?", "answer": "126 reps: 42 deadlifts, 42 air squats and 42 box jumps, plus the 1,742 m row."}, {"question": "Why is the row 1,742 meters?", "answer": "1st Lt. Damon Leehan was the 1,742nd soldier lost in Operation Enduring Freedom."}, {"question": "Who was Leehan?", "answer": "1st Lt. Damon Leehan, who was killed by an improvised explosive device on Aug. 14, 2011, while on a mission in Afghanistan. He served two tours of duty."}]'::jsonb,
   null),
