   'time',
   'Liam honors U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Liam J. Nevins, 32, of Middlebury, Vermont, who was assigned to the 5th Battalion, 19th Special Forces Group, at Fort Carson, Colorado. He was killed by small arms fire on Sept. 21, 2013, during combat operations in Paktia Province, Afghanistan. Friends remember him as a cut above when it came to fitness.

You start and finish with an 800 m run while carrying a plate (45 lb / 25 lb). In between you complete 100 toes-to-bar, 50 front squats (155 lb / 105 lb) and 10 rope climbs to 15 ft, split and ordered however you like. Your grip is the limit, because the toes-to-bar and rope climbs both use it. The second plate run then comes on tired arms and legs.',
   '[{"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hold the plate at your chest or on a shoulder and switch sides often. Run at an easy pace.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "100", "tip": "Small sets from the start. Kick your toes to the bar and keep a tight swing."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "50", "tip": "Elbows high, squat below parallel and drive up through your heels.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "10 to 15 ft", "tip": "Lock the rope with your feet and stand up. Climb down under control."}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Same carry as the first run. Shorten your stride and keep moving.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Split the middle work into small rounds", "Protect your grip for the rope climbs", "Switch the plate between hands on the runs"]'::jsonb,
   '["One way to split the middle is 10 rounds of 10 toes-to-bar, 5 front squats and 1 rope climb, which spreads out the grip work.", "Stop each toes-to-bar set a few reps before you fail, so your grip lasts for the rope.", "Use your feet on every rope climb, so your legs do the work and your arms just hold on.", "Clean the barbell from the floor for each set of front squats, and keep your elbows up so the bar stays on your shoulders.", "CrossFit does not say how to hold the plate on the runs, so carry it in whatever way you can hold for 800 m."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter plate, such as 25 lb / 15 lb, or run without one. Replace toes-to-bar with hanging knee raises, and cut the total to 50. Lower the front squats to 115 lb / 75 lb. Replace each rope climb with 3 lying-to-standing rope pulls or a climb to a lower height.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Liam workout?", "answer": "For time: run 800 m with a plate (45 lb / 25 lb), then 100 toes-to-bar, 50 front squats (155 lb / 105 lb) and 10 rope climbs to 15 ft, split as needed, then run 800 m with the plate."}, {"question": "Can I split the reps in Liam?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit says to partition the toes-to-bar, front squats and rope climbs as needed. Start and finish with the run."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Liam?", "answer": "160 reps: 100 toes-to-bar, 50 front squats and 10 rope climbs, plus 1,600 m of running with the plate."}, {"question": "Who was Liam?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Liam J. Nevins, 32, of Middlebury, Vermont, of the 19th Special Forces Group. He was killed by small arms fire on Sept. 21, 2013, in Paktia Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cq3nw7SceYY'),
