   'time',
   'Locke honors Matthew S. Locke, who died on Sept. 25, 2021, while trying to save someone''s life. He served in the Army National Guard and deployed to Afghanistan from May 2013 to February 2014. After returning home he worked in law enforcement with agencies including the McNairy County Sheriff''s Department, the Adamsville Police Department and the Hardin County Sheriff''s Department.

You row or run 565 m, complete 7 rounds of 9 deadlifts (185 lb / 125 lb), 25 push-ups and 21 box step-ups (24 in / 20 in), then row or run another 565 m. That adds up to 63 deadlifts, 175 push-ups and 147 step-ups. The push-ups add up fast, so plan small sets from round one.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "565 m run or row", "tip": "CrossFit allows a row or a run. Keep it easy at the start, because the rounds are long."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "7 rounds of 9", "tip": "Flat back, bar close, and lock out your hips at the top.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "7 rounds of 25", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top. Break into sets before you fail."}, {"name": "Box Step-Ups", "reps": "7 rounds of 21", "tip": "Whole foot on the box and stand all the way up. Switch legs as you need.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "565 m run or row", "tip": "The last effort. Use the same choice as your first one so the score compares."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time, and note whether you rowed or ran.',
   '["Pick row or run and use it for both", "Break the push-ups from round one", "Stand tall on every step-up"]'::jsonb,
   '["Choose the row or the run before you start and do the same for both, so your times compare later.", "Plan the 25 push-ups as sets such as 10, 8 and 7, with short breaks between them.", "Keep the deadlifts unbroken while you can, because 9 reps at this load is manageable for most athletes.", "On the step-ups, push through the heel on the box and do not push off the floor with your back foot.", "CrossFit does not say whether 21 step-ups means total or per leg, so count each step as one rep and note it."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 135 lb / 95 lb or less. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Use a lower box for the step-ups. Newer athletes can do 4 or 5 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Locke workout?", "answer": "For time: a 565 m row or run, then 7 rounds of 9 deadlifts (185 lb / 125 lb), 25 push-ups and 21 box step-ups (24 in / 20 in), then another 565 m row or run."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Locke?", "answer": "385 reps: 63 deadlifts, 175 push-ups and 147 box step-ups, plus 1,130 m of rowing or running."}, {"question": "Should I row or run?", "answer": "CrossFit allows either. Pick one and use it for both legs, and note which one you chose with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Locke?", "answer": "Matthew S. Locke, an Army National Guard veteran who deployed to Afghanistan and later served in law enforcement. He died on Sept. 25, 2021, while trying to save someone''s life."}]'::jsonb,
