   'Lorenzo honors Lorenzo Zanetti, 47, a CrossFit Level 2 Trainer and the owner of Mad Tortuga CrossFit in Rovereto, Italy. He died suddenly of a heart attack on Jan. 15 in Rovereto. Friends remember him as one of the strongest supporters of the Italian CrossFit community, and he kept coaching his members online when the COVID-19 pandemic closed his gym.

You run 1,000 m, complete 5 rounds of 15 push-ups, 20 medicine-ball cleans and 21 burpees, and finish with another 1,000 m run. CrossFit does not give a medicine-ball weight, so choose one you can clean for steady sets. The 105 burpees are what slow most people down, and they leave your legs heavy for the last run.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you could repeat at the end. The rounds are long."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "5 rounds of 15", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top. Break into sets early."}, {"name": "Medicine Ball Cleans", "reps": "5 rounds of 20", "tip": "Squat with the ball between your feet, then stand and pop it to your chest, landing in a squat. CrossFit does not list a weight."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "5 rounds of 21", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Find a rhythm you can hold."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Tired legs from the burpees. Shorten your stride and keep moving."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time, and note your medicine-ball weight.',
   '["Pick a ball weight and note it", "Pace the burpees, do not race them", "Keep the first run easy"]'::jsonb,
   '["Split the 15 push-ups into sets such as 8 and 7 before your chest gives out.", "On the ball cleans, keep the ball close and use your hips, not your arms.", "Set up the ball and your burpee spot next to each other so you move straight from one to the next.", "Breathe out as your chest hits the floor on each burpee and keep a steady pace.", "Use the last run to empty the tank, because nothing comes after it."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter medicine ball. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Cut the burpees to 15 per round, or do 3 or 4 rounds. Shorten each run to 600 m.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Lorenzo workout?", "answer": "For time: run 1,000 m, then 5 rounds of 15 push-ups, 20 medicine-ball cleans and 21 burpees, then run 1,000 m."}, {"question": "What weight is the medicine ball?", "answer": "CrossFit does not list one. Pick a ball you can clean in steady sets and note the weight with your time."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Lorenzo?", "answer": "280 reps: 75 push-ups, 100 ball cleans and 105 burpees, plus 2,000 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Lorenzo?", "answer": "Lorenzo Zanetti, 47, a CrossFit Level 2 Trainer and owner of Mad Tortuga CrossFit in Rovereto, Italy. He died suddenly of a heart attack on Jan. 15."}]'::jsonb,
