You run 400 m seven times. Between the runs you do 15 clean and jerks (155 lb / 105 lb), 30 toes-to-bar, 45 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb to 10 ft / 9 ft), 45 kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb), 30 ring dips and 15 front-rack lunges. The runs give you a short break from each station, but they add up to 2,800 m. Every station hits a different part of the body.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Seven runs in all. Hold a pace you can repeat."}, {"name": "Clean and Jerks", "reps": "15", "tip": "Clean to your shoulders, then dip and drive overhead. Quick singles are fine.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Shake out your arms and grip."}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "30", "tip": "Small sets and a tight swing. Kick your toes to the bar."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Breathe and get ready for the wall balls."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "45", "tip": "Squat below parallel and hit the target every rep.", "rx_men": "20 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Settle your breathing before the swings."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "45", "tip": "Snap your hips and swing the bell overhead.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Loosen your shoulders for the dips."}, {"name": "Ring Dips", "reps": "30", "tip": "Lower until your shoulders are below your elbows, then lock out at the top."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "One station left. Keep moving."}, {"name": "Barbell Lunges", "reps": "15", "tip": "Hold the bar in the front rack, elbows up, and touch your back knee to the floor each rep.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "The last run. Empty the tank."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Keep the seven runs at an even pace", "Break the toes-to-bar and dips early", "Stay tall on the front-rack lunges"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set every station close to your running route so each one starts as soon as you get back.", "On the clean and jerks, take quick singles with a short breath between each rep.", "Break the 45 wall balls and 45 swings into sets you can hold, such as 15, 15 and 15.", "On the ring dips, keep the rings close to your body and lock out fully at the top.", "CrossFit lists the lunges as front-rack weighted lunges with the barbell, but does not say if 15 means total or per leg; count each step as one rep and note it."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 115 lb / 75 lb or less. Replace toes-to-bar with hanging knee raises and ring dips with bar dips or bench dips. Use a lighter medicine ball and kettlebell. Shorten each run to 200 m if needed.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Luke workout?", "answer": "For time: run 400 m, 15 clean and jerks, run 400 m, 30 toes-to-bar, run 400 m, 45 wall balls, run 400 m, 45 kettlebell swings, run 400 m, 30 ring dips, run 400 m, 15 front-rack lunges, run 400 m."}, {"question": "What are the Rx loads for Luke?", "answer": "A 155 lb / 105 lb barbell, a 20 lb / 14 lb medicine ball to a 10 ft / 9 ft target and a 53 lb / 35 lb kettlebell."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Luke?", "answer": "180 reps: 15 clean and jerks, 30 toes-to-bar, 45 wall balls, 45 kettlebell swings, 30 ring dips and 15 lunges, plus 2,800 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Luke?", "answer": "Marine Staff Sgt. Leon H. Lucas Jr., 32, of Wilson, North Carolina. He died on Aug. 1, 2011, in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, of injuries from an enemy grenade attack."}]'::jsonb,
