You complete 6 rounds of a 300 m shuttle run, 16 deadlifts and 6 hang power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb for both), with 2 minutes of rest between rounds. The turns on the shuttle run make it harder than a straight 300 m, and the heavy cleans come right after 16 deadlifts.',
   '[{"name": "Shuttle Run", "reps": "300 m", "tip": "CrossFit lists the 300 m as 50 m out and back x 6, then 100 m out and back x 3. Stay low on the turns."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "16", "tip": "Flat back, bar close, and stand all the way up. Break into 2 sets if you need to.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Hang Power Cleans", "reps": "6", "tip": "Start with the bar above your knees, jump and catch it on your shoulders above parallel.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "2 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Rest between rounds. Walk, breathe and set up for the next shuttle."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time. CrossFit does not say whether the rest periods count, so note whether your time includes them.',
   '["Use the 2 minute rest to recover fully", "Stay low through the shuttle turns", "Grip the bar tight for the cleans"]'::jsonb,
   '["Mark your shuttle distances before you start. CrossFit''s note on the shuttle is unclear, so make sure each round adds up to 300 m.", "Plant your outside foot and stay low on each turn instead of running past the line.", "Split the 16 deadlifts into 8 and 8 if the load is heavy for you.", "Rest your hands for a breath after the deadlifts so your grip is ready for the hang power cleans.", "Start each round when your rest ends, so every round has the same work and rest."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 135 lb / 95 lb or less. Shorten the shuttle run to 200 m. Newer athletes can do 4 rounds.',
