   'Manuel honors Italian Army Capt. Manuel Fiorito, 27, of Verona, Italy, who served with the Italian 2nd Alpine Regiment. He was killed on May 5, 2006, when a roadside bomb detonated near his vehicle in Kabul, Afghanistan, after tending to wounded men. He was posthumously awarded the Silver Medal of Military Valor and was a pioneer in bringing CrossFit to the Italian military.

Wearing a weight vest or body armor, you complete 5 rounds of 3 minutes of rope climbs, 2 minutes of squats, 2 minutes of push-ups and 3 minutes to run 400 m. You rest for whatever is left of the run''s 3 minutes, so each round takes 10 minutes. The rope climbs under load are the hardest part, and they wear out your grip.',
   '[{"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "3 min", "tip": "As many climbs as you can. Lock the rope with your feet and climb down under control.", "rx_men": "Weight vest", "rx_women": "Weight vest"}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "2 min", "tip": "Hip crease below the knee, stand tall. Find a rhythm you can hold for the whole 2 minutes.", "rx_men": "Weight vest", "rx_women": "Weight vest"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "2 min", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top. Short sets with quick breaks.", "rx_men": "Weight vest", "rx_women": "Weight vest"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m within 3 min", "tip": "Run 400 m. Rest for what is left of the 3 minutes, then start the next round.", "rx_men": "Weight vest", "rx_women": "Weight vest"}]'::jsonb,
   'CrossFit does not say how to score Manuel. Count your total rope climbs, squats and push-ups across the 5 rounds, and note your vest weight.',
   '["Pace the first round of rope climbs", "Use your feet on every climb", "Run fast enough to earn some rest"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not give a vest weight or a rope height, so pick ones you can use for all 5 rounds and note them.", "Climb at a steady pace in the first round, because your grip has to last for 15 minutes of climbing.", "Strap the vest tight and high so it does not bounce on the run.", "Keep moving on the squats and push-ups, even if that means very short sets.", "Run the 400 m at a pace that leaves you some rest before the next rope climbs."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest or use a lighter one. Replace rope climbs with lying-to-standing rope pulls or climbs to a lower height. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Do 3 rounds instead of 5.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Manuel workout?", "answer": "5 rounds of 3 minutes of rope climbs, 2 minutes of squats, 2 minutes of push-ups and 3 minutes to run 400 m, resting for the rest of the 3 minutes after the run. Wear a weight vest or body armor."}, {"question": "How is Manuel scored?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Count your total rope climbs, squats and push-ups across the 5 rounds, and note your vest weight."}, {"question": "How heavy is the vest?", "answer": "CrossFit says to wear a weight vest or body armor but does not give a weight. Use one you can wear for 50 minutes and note it with your score."}, {"question": "Who was Manuel?", "answer": "Italian Army Capt. Manuel Fiorito, 27, of Verona, of the 2nd Alpine Regiment. He was killed on May 5, 2006, when a roadside bomb detonated near his vehicle in Kabul, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
