   'Marco honors U.S. Marine Cpl. Marc T. Ryan, 25, of Gloucester City, New Jersey, a weapons specialist with the 2nd Battalion, 5th Marine Regiment, 1st Marine Division, at Camp Pendleton, California. He died on Nov. 15, 2004, from a roadside bomb in Ramadi, Iraq.

You complete 3 rounds of 21 pull-ups, 15 handstand push-ups and 9 thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb). That adds up to 63 pull-ups, 45 handstand push-ups and 27 thrusters. The pull-ups and handstand push-ups tire your upper body first, so the thrusters feel heavier than usual. Your shoulders get very little rest.',
   '[{"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "21", "tip": "Chin over the bar each rep. Break into sets before your grip fails."}, {"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "Head to the floor or mat and lock out at the top. Break early."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "9", "tip": "Squat below parallel and drive the bar overhead in one move.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the pull-ups early", "Short sets on the handstand push-ups", "Take the thrusters in 2 or 3 sets"]'::jsonb,
   '["Plan the 21 pull-ups as sets such as 8, 7 and 6 in the first round.", "Rest briefly before the handstand push-ups, because a missed rep costs more than a short pause.", "Set up a mat or folded pad at the wall so every rep touches the same spot.", "Use your legs on the thrusters so your tired shoulders only have to finish the press.", "Expect round 3 to be the slowest, and keep the breaks short."]'::jsonb,
   'Use banded or jumping pull-ups. Replace handstand push-ups with pike push-ups or dumbbell push presses. Lower the thrusters to 95 lb / 65 lb or less.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Marco workout?", "answer": "3 rounds for time of 21 pull-ups, 15 handstand push-ups and 9 thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Marco?", "answer": "135 reps: 63 pull-ups, 45 handstand push-ups and 27 thrusters."}, {"question": "What if I cannot do handstand push-ups?", "answer": "Do pike push-ups or dumbbell push presses instead, and note the change with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Marco?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Cpl. Marc T. Ryan, 25, of Gloucester City, New Jersey, a weapons specialist with the 2nd Battalion, 5th Marines. He died on Nov. 15, 2004, from a roadside bomb in Ramadi, Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
