   'full-body',
   array['barbell','pullUpBar','bodyweight']::text[],
   'rounds_reps',
   'Marston honors Special Warfare Operator 1st Class William Blake Marston, 31, of Concord, New Hampshire, who served six years in the Navy and was assigned to an East Coast-based SEAL Team. He died on Jan. 10, 2015, in DeLand, Florida, during military parachute training.

You complete as many rounds as you can in 20 minutes of 1 deadlift (405 lb / 275 lb), 10 toes-to-bar and 15 bar-facing burpees. The single deadlift is very heavy, so each rep needs a full setup. The burpees and toes-to-bar then keep your heart rate high, which makes the next heavy pull harder.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "1", "tip": "One heavy rep. Set a flat back, take the slack out of the bar and push the floor away.", "rx_men": "405 lb", "rx_women": "275 lb"}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "10", "tip": "Tight swing and small sets. Kick your toes to the bar."}, {"name": "Bar-Facing Burpees", "reps": "15", "tip": "Face the bar, chest to the floor, then jump over it with both feet."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
   '["Take a breath and set up for every deadlift", "Keep the burpees steady", "Break the toes-to-bar early"]'::jsonb,
   '["Use the same barbell for the deadlift and the burpees so you never move between stations.", "Never rush the deadlift. A safe, set-up rep is worth more than a few seconds.", "Jump over the long side of the bar and land with both feet together.", "Break the 10 toes-to-bar into 5 and 5 from the start to save your grip for the deadlift.", "Find a burpee pace you can hold for 20 minutes rather than sprinting the first rounds."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to a weight you can lift safely when tired, such as 275 lb / 185 lb or less. Replace toes-to-bar with hanging knee raises. Do regular burpees or step over the bar.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Marston workout?", "answer": "As many rounds and reps as possible in 20 minutes of 1 deadlift (405 lb / 275 lb), 10 toes-to-bar and 15 bar-facing burpees."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round of Marston?", "answer": "26 reps: 1 deadlift, 10 toes-to-bar and 15 bar-facing burpees."}, {"question": "Is 405 lb required?", "answer": "That is the Rx load. Use a weight you can lift safely when tired, and note it with your score."}, {"question": "Who was Marston?", "answer": "Special Warfare Operator 1st Class William Blake Marston, 31, of Concord, New Hampshire, a Navy SEAL. He died on Jan. 10, 2015, in DeLand, Florida, during military parachute training."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Konznsv6lgA'),
  ('Martin',
