   '35–50 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['rower','barbell','bodyweight','pullUpBar','wallBall']::text[],
   'time',
   'Martin honors British Army Pvt. Martin Simon George Bell of the 2nd Battalion, Parachute Regiment. He was killed on Jan. 25, 2011, near the village of Spoor Kalay in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, by an improvised explosive device as he moved to help an injured comrade. Before joining the Parachute Regiment he served three years as a Police Community Support Officer in West Yorkshire.

You do this one with a partner. It is a chipper of a 2,000 m row, 100 bodyweight deadlifts, 50 thrusters (95 lb / 65 lb), a 1,000 m row, 100 hand-release push-ups, 50 pull-ups, a 500 m row, 100 sit-ups and 100 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb). The rows get shorter as you go, and how well you and your partner swap decides your time.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "2,000 m", "tip": "Split into short turns so both partners stay fresh."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "100", "tip": "Load the bar to your bodyweight. Flat back and stand all the way up.", "rx_men": "Bodyweight", "rx_women": "Bodyweight"}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "50", "tip": "Squat below parallel and drive the bar overhead in one move.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Row", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Short turns again, and swap quickly."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Chest to the floor, lift your hands, then press back up."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chin over the bar each rep. Short sets and quick swaps."}, {"name": "Row", "reps": "500 m", "tip": "The last row. Go hard."}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Shoulders to the floor and hands to your feet."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "100", "tip": "Squat below parallel and hit the target every rep.", "rx_men": "20 lb", "rx_women": "14 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time.',
   '["Swap often, before either of you slows down", "Plan a bar for each partner''s bodyweight", "Keep the rows in short turns"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not say how partners split Martin, so split the work however you like and use the same plan if you repeat it.", "If you and your partner weigh very different amounts, you may need two bars or a plate change for the deadlifts.", "Set a rep count for each swap, such as 10 reps each, so no one has to think about it.", "CrossFit does not give a wall-ball target height, so use the usual 10 ft / 9 ft target and note it.", "Keep the rower damper and seat settings marked so each swap takes only a few seconds."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 75% of bodyweight or less, and the thrusters to 65 lb / 45 lb. Use regular push-ups or push-ups from your knees. Use banded or jumping pull-ups. Cut every rep count in half for a shorter version.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Martin workout?", "answer": "A partner workout for time: 2,000 m row, 100 bodyweight deadlifts, 50 thrusters (95 lb / 65 lb), 1,000 m row, 100 hand-release push-ups, 50 pull-ups, 500 m row, 100 sit-ups and 100 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb)."}, {"question": "How do partners split Martin?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Split the work however you like, and use the same plan each time you repeat the workout so your times compare."}, {"question": "What does bodyweight deadlift mean?", "answer": "Load the barbell to your own bodyweight. If partners weigh different amounts, each lifts their own load."}, {"question": "Who was Martin?", "answer": "British Army Pvt. Martin Simon George Bell of the 2nd Battalion, Parachute Regiment. He was killed on Jan. 25, 2011, near Spoor Kalay in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, as he moved to help an injured comrade."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BvqKBkTJFBw'),
  ('Matt 16',
   'matt-16',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   'For Time',
   '25–35 min',
