   'full-body',
   array['barbell','running']::text[],
   'time',
   'Matt 16 honors U.S. Army Chief Warrant Officer Matt Ruffner, 34, of Tafford, Pennsylvania, assigned to the 1st Attack Reconnaissance Battalion, 104th Aviation Regiment, Pennsylvania National Guard, at Fort Indiantown Gap. He died on April 9, 2013, in the Pachir Wa Agam district of Afghanistan, from injuries sustained when his AH-64 Apache helicopter crashed.

You complete 3 sets of 16 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb), 16 hang power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb) and 16 push presses (135 lb / 95 lb), with an 800 m run between sets. Each lift in the set gets lighter, but your grip and back get more tired. The runs give your hands a break, but not your lungs.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "16", "tip": "Flat back, bar close, and stand all the way up. Break into 2 or 3 sets.", "rx_men": "275 lb", "rx_women": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Hang Power Cleans", "reps": "16", "tip": "Bar above the knees, jump and catch it on your shoulders above parallel.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Push Press", "reps": "16", "tip": "Dip and drive with your legs, then lock out overhead.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Shake out your grip and breathe."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "16", "tip": "Same setup as the first set. Stay patient.", "rx_men": "275 lb", "rx_women": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Hang Power Cleans", "reps": "16", "tip": "Small sets with short breaks.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Push Press", "reps": "16", "tip": "Use your legs so your shoulders last.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "One more set after this run."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "16", "tip": "Last set. Keep your back flat.", "rx_men": "275 lb", "rx_women": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Hang Power Cleans", "reps": "16", "tip": "Grip will be tired. Use quick singles if needed.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Push Press", "reps": "16", "tip": "The finish. Lock out every rep.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Load three bars if you can", "Break the deadlifts before your back rounds", "Use the runs to rest your grip"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up three barbells, one for each lift, so you do not change plates between movements.", "Plan the 16 deadlifts as sets such as 6, 5 and 5 to keep your back flat.", "Drop to quick singles on the hang power cleans when your grip starts to fade.", "On the push press, dip straight down and keep your elbows in front of the bar.", "Run at a steady pace so you come back ready to lift, not gasping for air."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the loads to 185 lb / 125 lb for the deadlift, 135 lb / 95 lb for the clean and 95 lb / 65 lb for the push press, or less. Cut each set to 10 reps. Shorten the runs to 400 m.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Matt 16 workout?", "answer": "For time: 16 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb), 16 hang power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb) and 16 push presses (135 lb / 95 lb), run 800 m, repeat the three lifts, run 800 m, then repeat the three lifts once more."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Matt 16?", "answer": "144 reps: 48 deadlifts, 48 hang power cleans and 48 push presses, plus 1,600 m of running."}, {"question": "Do I need three barbells?", "answer": "It helps, because each lift has its own load. With one bar, change plates between lifts and expect a slower time."}, {"question": "Who was Matt 16?", "answer": "U.S. Army Chief Warrant Officer Matt Ruffner, 34, of the Pennsylvania National Guard. He died on April 9, 2013, in Afghanistan, from injuries sustained when his AH-64 Apache helicopter crashed."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LK875J0LN-s'),
  ('Maxim 56',
   'maxim-56',
   'hero',
