   'For Time',
   'For Time (Partner)',
   '50–75 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['bodyweight','running']::text[],
   'time',
   'Maxim 56 honors two decorated Apache pilots, Chief Warrant Officer 2 Kirk Fuchigami, 25, and Chief Warrant Officer 2 David Knadle, 33, of the 1st Battalion, 227th Aviation Regiment, 1st Air Cavalry Brigade, 1st Cavalry Division, at Fort Hood, Texas. They died on Nov. 20, 2019, in a helicopter crash while providing security for troops on the ground in Afghanistan''s Logar province.

You do this one with a partner. Each partner starts with a 56 second handstand hold or wall sit. Then each athlete completes 56 burpees, 56 four-count flutter kicks, 56 walking lunges, 56 hand-release push-ups and 56 air squats. You finish with a 5,600 m run. The bodyweight work is long, and the run is the hardest part.',
   '[{"name": "Handstand Hold", "reps": "56 sec (or wall sit)", "tip": "Each partner holds a handstand or a wall sit for 56 seconds."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "56 each", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Find a steady rhythm."}, {"name": "Flutter Kicks", "reps": "56 each (4-count)", "tip": "Lower back pressed down, legs straight. One rep is four kicks, left, right, left, right."}, {"name": "Walking Lunges", "reps": "56 each", "tip": "Back knee touches the floor and you stand tall each step."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "56 each", "tip": "Chest to the floor, lift your hands, then press back up."}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "56 each", "tip": "Hip crease below the knee and stand tall."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "5,600 m", "tip": "The cash-out. Settle into a pace you can hold for the whole distance."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time.',
   '["Pace the burpees, they come first", "Count flutter kicks in fours", "Start the long run slowly"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not say whether partners work at the same time or take turns, or whether the 5,600 m run is done by each partner or shared, so decide before you start and note it.", "Pick the wall sit if you cannot hold a handstand for 56 seconds, and note your choice.", "Break the 56 burpees and push-ups into sets such as 4 sets of 14.", "Keep your lower back pressed into the floor on the flutter kicks to protect it.", "Run the first kilometer slower than feels needed, because 5,600 m is a long way after 280 reps."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut each movement to 28 reps and shorten the run to 2,800 m. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Do the wall sit instead of the handstand hold.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Maxim 56 workout?", "answer": "A partner workout for time. Each partner does a 56 second handstand hold or wall sit. Then each athlete completes 56 burpees, 56 flutter kicks (4-count), 56 walking lunges, 56 hand-release push-ups and 56 air squats, and the team finishes with a 5,600 m run."}, {"question": "Does each partner run 5,600 m?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say whether each partner runs the full distance or you share it. Choose one and note it with your time."}, {"question": "How many reps does each athlete do?", "answer": "280 reps: 56 of each of the five movements, plus the 56 second hold."}, {"question": "Who is Maxim 56 named for?", "answer": "Chief Warrant Officer 2 Kirk Fuchigami, 25, and Chief Warrant Officer 2 David Knadle, 33, Apache pilots with the 1st Cavalry Division. They died on Nov. 20, 2019, in a helicopter crash in Afghanistan''s Logar province."}]'::jsonb,
   null),
  ('Maxton',
   'maxton',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '13 Rounds For Time',
   '40–60 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['pullUpBar','box','bodyweight','weightedVest']::text[],
   'time',
   'Maxton honors Navy Corpsman Maxton Soviak, 22, one of the 13 U.S. service members killed in the attack outside the Kabul airport in Afghanistan on Aug. 26, 2021. He was an avid CrossFit athlete who trained at CrossFit Hita, CrossFit Latte Stone and Custom Fitness Guam, and this workout includes some of his favorite movements.

Wearing a weight vest (20 lb / 14 lb), you complete 13 rounds of 8 strict pull-ups, 26 box step-ups (24 in / 20 in) and 21 burpees. That adds up to 104 strict pull-ups, 338 step-ups and 273 burpees. It is a long grind, and the strict pull-ups get very hard in the vest.',
   '[{"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "8", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull your chin over the bar.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Box Step-Ups", "reps": "26", "tip": "Whole foot on the box and stand all the way up. Switch legs as you need.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "21", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Keep a steady rhythm.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time. Wear the vest for the whole workout.',
   '["Break the strict pull-ups from round one", "Steady pace on the step-ups", "Plan for 13 rounds, not 3"]'::jsonb,
   '["Strap the vest tight and high so it does not shift on the burpees.", "Split the 8 strict pull-ups into sets such as 3, 3 and 2 before your arms give out.", "On the step-ups, drive through the heel on the box and do not push off the floor with your back foot.", "CrossFit does not say whether 26 step-ups means total or per leg, so count each step as one rep and note it.", "Find a burpee pace you could hold for all 13 rounds, and check your time after each round."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest or use a lighter one. Use banded pull-ups or ring rows. Use a lower box. Do 7 rounds, or cut the reps in half.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Maxton workout?", "answer": "Wearing a weight vest (20 lb / 14 lb), complete 13 rounds for time of 8 strict pull-ups, 26 box step-ups (24 in / 20 in) and 21 burpees."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Maxton?", "answer": "715 reps: 104 strict pull-ups, 338 box step-ups and 273 burpees."}, {"question": "Do I wear the vest for the whole workout?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit lists the vest as part of the Rx, so wear it for every round. Drop it or go lighter to scale."}, {"question": "Who was Maxton?", "answer": "Navy Corpsman Maxton Soviak, 22, an avid CrossFit athlete. He was killed in the attack outside the Kabul airport in Afghanistan on Aug. 26, 2021."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OhkNyPvamIo');
  get diagnostics n = row_count;
  if n <> 13 then raise exception 'expected % inserts', 13; end if;
